# homedepot-scraper — configuration
# =================================
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is NOT, so it
# must never hold a real value. env_config.py reads exactly the four names
# below and warns about anything else, which catches a typo like
# TWO_CAPTCHA_KEY before it becomes a confusing empty run.
#
# Credentials live HERE and nowhere else — never on a command line. `ps` reads
# argv, and argv lands in shell history and in CI logs.

# 2captcha.com API key. Used by the captcha solver fallback, by
# fingerprint_client.py and by tools/browser_profile_client.py.
# NOT needed for an ordinary run: the wall on this site is not a captcha.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=

# An HTTP proxy, as a single URL: http://user:pass@host:port
#
# THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL, AND IT MUST BE A US EXIT. Measured 2026-09-22 from a
# Moscow residential address: every URL on www.homedepot.com answered HTTP 403
# in 367 bytes, /robots.txt included. Through a US residential exit the same
# URLs answered 200.
#
# A US address is necessary and NOT sufficient — the request also has to look
# like a browser. http_scraper.py sends the header set that was measured to
# work; a bare user agent got 403 from the same US exit in the same minute.
#
# Exits are scored individually and the hit rate moves. Measured over six
# session-pinned exits in one minute: four served the full listing, one served
# Akamai's interstitial, one timed out. `--proxy-sessions N` turns one
# credential into N session-pinned exits and `--proxy-block-retries` decides
# how many times a refused page may move to a different one.
HOMEDEPOT_PROXY=

# A Scraping Browser API CDP endpoint, for the three browser engines only.
# http_scraper.py and catalog_walk.py do not use it.
#
#   ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222
#
# `country-us` is what makes the exit American; `pid-` is a profile with
# persistent cookies. A profile allows ONE live connection — a second run on
# the same pid fails with `profile_locked`, so reuse pids rather than minting
# one per run.
#
# Mint one for THIS repo rather than reusing a sibling's:
#   python3 tools/browser_profile_client.py accounts
#   python3 tools/browser_profile_client.py use --account-id N --write-env
#
# This is the transport that actually clears Akamai's interstitial, because a
# real browser executes the sensor script. It is the recommended path.
HOMEDEPOT_CDP_ENDPOINT=

# Optional. Overrides the URL an engine would otherwise build.
HOMEDEPOT_URL=
